  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In a test, there are NNN problems, each carrying XXX marks.\n\nIn each problem, Chef either received XXX marks or 000 marks.\n\nDetermine whether is it possible for Chef to achieve **exactly** YYY marks.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three integers N,X,N, X,N,X, and YYY, the number of problems, the maximum score for each problem, and the score Chef wants.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output `YES` if Chef can achieve exactly YYY marks, `NO` otherwise.\n\n\nYou can print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase. For example, the strings `Yes`, `YES`, `yes`, and `yEs`, are all considered identical.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10",
      "1≤X≤101 \\leq X \\leq 101≤X≤10",
      "0≤Y≤1000 \\leq Y \\leq 1000≤Y≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n1 8 4\n3 6 12\n4 5 0\n10 10 100\n8 5 36",
        "output": "NO\nYES\nYES\nYES\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There is no way for Chef to score exactly 444 marks.\nTest case 222: Chef can score 121212 marks by receiving 666 marks in 222 problems and 000 marks in 111 problem.\nTest case 333: Chef can score 000 marks by receiving 000 marks in each of the 444 problems.\nTest case 444: Chef can score 100100100 marks by receiving 101010 marks in each of the 101010 problems.\nTest case 555: There is no way for Chef to score exactly 363636 marks."
      }
    ]
  },
